# mrustc.answers: byte-seal pins for packages/mrustc. Currently unpinned.
#
# build.sh runs `sha256sum -c` on this file from ${OUTPUT_DIR} as soon as it contains a line
# matching `^<64 hex>  <path>`; no code change is needed to arm it.
#
# To seal, once two independent builds have produced byte-identical output:
#   cd ${OUTPUT_DIR} && sha256sum usr/bin/mrustc usr/bin/minicargo
# and paste the lines below, uncommented, in `sha256sum` format (two spaces).
#
# usr/share/mrustc/** is not pinned: copies of Local inputs and a constant-only BUILDINFO,
# already covered by their input shas.
#
# Nondeterminism status of the two binaries:
#   - Makefile:190 VERSION_BUILDTIME + 4 git shell-outs: patched, proven in-build by a
#     later-wall-clock version.o rebuild + byte-compare
#   - .note.gnu.build-id: suppressed (-Wl,--build-id=none)
#   - debug info paths: stable (cwd is always /build/...)
#   - --add-gnu-debuglink CRC: derived, therefore stable
#   - ar member mtimes in bin/*.a: do not reach the linked binaries
# Makefile:190 is the only date/git shell-out in Makefile, minicargo.mk, tools/*/Makefile and
# run_rustc/Makefile.
#
# UNPINNED
# usr/bin/mrustc
# usr/bin/minicargo
